    <dimen name="marker_width">3dp</dimen>

    <!-- The D-pad focus contour, everywhere one is drawn: the three button styles in themes.xml, the
         picker row, the slider thumb, the skip pill and the chrome over video. One number, because it used
         to be five literal 2dp's reached by three different paths, and they did not agree — Utils.dpToPx
         truncates, so the row's "2dp" arrived 50% thinner than the buttons' identical 2dp.

         The same 2dp on a television, where it used to be 4dp. A focus mark is read, not measured: 2dp is
         4px on a 1080p set, which subtends about 3 arcmin at three metres — three times the eye's limit —
         while 4dp around a 44dp tile is a ninth of the tile and reads as a slab, not a line. Contrast does
         the carrying instead: the contour is always drawn on a plate, never on the picture. -->
    <dimen name="focus_ring_width">2dp</dimen>

    <dimen name="level_bar_width">6dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="level_bar_height">160dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="level_bar_margin">28dp</dimen>
</resources>